  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Magnetic Field Inside Solenoid is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><mi>I</mi></math></p><p>Velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#957;</mi></math>&nbsp;has given&nbsp;to the electron&nbsp;</p><p>So, Magnetic Force</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>&#957;</mi><mi>B</mi></math></p><p>as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are perpendicular.</p><p>In a magnetic field, charge will move on a circular path. Here, If radius is just less than or equal to radius of solenoid then the electron does not hit the surface.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>&#957;</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#957;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>a</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>&#957;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi>S</mi><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>n</mi><mi>I</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></math><br />&nbsp;</p>",
